-- purdue-pharma (2026-11-16, Avik): the record, each fact with its warrant:
-- * Purdue Pharma (owned by the Sackler family) launched OxyContin in 1996. Its affiliate Purdue
--   Frederick and three executives pleaded guilty to misbranding OxyContin in 2007; Purdue pleaded guilty
--   in 2020 to three federal felonies, a plea accepted by a New Jersey federal judge in April 2026
--   (Bloomberg Law, 2026-04-28).
-- * Purdue's chapter 11 (S.D.N.Y. 19-23649, filed 2019-09-15, Judge Sean Lane) ended with a plan
--   confirmed 2025-11-18 after the Supreme Court struck the Sacklers' nonconsensual releases (Harrington
--   v. Purdue, 2024): about $7.4 billion, the Sacklers paying $6.5 to 7 billion over 15 years ($1.5
--   billion on the effective date), the family out of the company. Effective in spring 2026; on
--   2026-05-01 the operations passed to Knoa Pharma LLC, owned by the Knoa Foundation (a 501(c)(4)).
-- * The Sackler name was on museums and universities worldwide (removed by the Met, the Louvre, the
--   Guggenheim, Tufts and others since 2019). Tel Aviv University's Sackler Faculty of Medicine is named
--   for the gift of Arthur, Mortimer and Raymond Sackler in the 1970s, before OxyContin existed;
--   Arthur Sackler died in 1987, and his heirs sold his share of Purdue to his brothers before OxyContin.
